# NEGATIVE PROBE (issue #115 leaf). Identical to structure.cm EXCEPT the boundary
# declaration drops `measure_only` (`boundary note "…"` instead of
# `boundary measure_only note "…"`). The measure-only boundary is load-bearing
# (STRUCT-REPAIR-001 / parent RCM-BOUNDARY-001: the CM observes and emits findings;
# it moves, renames, and deletes nothing). The surface makes the measure-only
# boundary structurally mandatory, so the front-end REJECTS this source at compile
# time — it never emits a projection. General over every aspect leaf.

cm tsc.repository-coherence.structure v0.2 (repo, policy) -> AspectReceipt {

  question "At a given commit, does every tracked artifact have exactly one clear place, name, owner, lifecycle, and relationship to the rest of the repository — judged against repository-planes, never against the CM's own taste."

  profile "repository-planes-v1.1"

  statuses COHERENT_WITHIN_DECLARED_SCOPE, DEFECTS_FOUND, UNDERDETERMINED, INCOMPLETE_OBSERVATION, CM_EXECUTION_FAILED
  status_mapping
    | COHERENT_WITHIN_DECLARED_SCOPE -> PASS
    | DEFECTS_FOUND                  -> DEFECT
    | UNDERDETERMINED                -> INCOMPLETE
    | INCOMPLETE_OBSERVATION         -> INCOMPLETE
    | CM_EXECUTION_FAILED            -> FAILED

  input repository_snapshot: "the tracked tree at one exact commit (git ls-files)"
  input policy_snapshot: "repository-planes ADR pinned at a commit (the sole placement/naming/function/lifecycle authority)"
  input exclusions: "the do-not-touch set (.cdd/ .cn-sigma/ heldout/) + build/agent/infra paths, not content-classified"

  step 1: "Enumerate all tracked paths in scope (git ls-files, minus exclusions)." checks [STRUCT-EXCLUDE-001]
  step 2: "Classify each path against the policy (plane, canonical home, docs reader-intent taxonomy, ownership, lifecycle)." checks [STRUCT-PLANE-001, STRUCT-RULE-001, STRUCT-CANON-001, STRUCT-NAME-001, STRUCT-DOCSET-001, STRUCT-FUNC-001, STRUCT-OWNER-001, STRUCT-MIXED-001, STRUCT-HISTLABEL-001, STRUCT-DERIVED-001]
  step 3: "Record violations where policy decides." checks []
  step 4: "Refuse (UNDERDETERMINED) where policy is silent." checks [STRUCT-REFUSE-001]
  step 5: "For every move/split/delete candidate, enumerate all live consumers (consumer-search contract)." checks [STRUCT-CONSUMER-001]
  step 6: "Emit the plane manifest, findings, refusals, and consumer graph." checks []

  decide
    | FAILED     when "FAILED — derivation.failed_mechanical_checks is non-empty (a required mechanical check could not execute), OR derivation.move_candidates_missing_search is non-empty (some finding has move_candidate==true and consumer_search==null)."
    | INCOMPLETE when "INCOMPLETE — derivation.heuristic_searches is non-empty (some consumer_search.search_strength is in derivation.incomplete_search_strengths, i.e. 'heuristic'; 'complete' and 'complete_within_bound' both count as COMPLETE), OR every finding has destination_resolved==false (derivation.unresolved_destinations == all findings)."
    | DEFECT     when "DEFECT — at least one finding establishes a policy violation (findings non-empty; derivation.findings_establishing_defect non-empty)."
    otherwise PASS

  # The 15 stable STRUCT-* requirements (id · claim · ADR clause · class · severity).
  requirement STRUCT-PLANE-001 "Every tracked path resolves to exactly one root plane; no path is a peer to the six planes or spans two." class mechanical severity P0 adr "Target planes (root)"
  requirement STRUCT-RULE-001 "Each path's plane is the one the decision rule selects (bind→spec, run→src, prove→conformance, still change→research, help a person→docs, automate→scripts)." class "mechanical + semantic" severity P0 adr "Decision rule"
  requirement STRUCT-CANON-001 "Every artifact the ADR program-maps give a canonical home sits at that home." class mechanical severity P0 adr "Program maps"
  requirement STRUCT-NAME-001 "Documentation is filed by reader intent; the α/β/γ role grammar is never used as a filing taxonomy." class "mechanical + semantic" severity P1 adr "Docs reader-intent taxonomy (\"α/β/γ … never a filing taxonomy\")"
  requirement STRUCT-DOCSET-001 "The eight reader-intent folders are the exhaustive set of docs/ subfolders; a docs/ subfolder outside them is a defect to rehome." class "mechanical + semantic" severity P1 adr "Amendments (v1.1) §1"
  requirement STRUCT-FUNC-001 "No plane is a single-occupant or premature catch-all standing in for a real home." class semantic severity P1 adr "Iteration 3 (\"…not a single-occupant config/ plane\")"
  requirement STRUCT-OWNER-001 "Each artifact has one authoritative home; no duplicate live copies." class mechanical severity P0 adr "Decision (organize by plane) + Program maps"
  requirement STRUCT-CONSUMER-001 "Each move/split/delete finding enumerates the artifact's live consumers via the consumer-search contract — surfaces searched, search strength, consumer set, digest, unsearched surfaces; a relocation that breaks a consumer without rehoming its reference is not coherent." class "mechanical + semantic" severity P0 adr "Invariants any move commit must preserve (\"targets resolve; conformance validator exits 0 …; no document's meaning changes\")"
  requirement STRUCT-MIXED-001 "No live directory mixes live-mutable content with frozen, snapshot, or archived content." class "mechanical + semantic" severity P0 adr "Migration state (frozen snapshots preserved intact)"
  requirement STRUCT-HISTLABEL-001 "Historical/archived/frozen material retained on the live tree carries a lifecycle label (banner or marker)." class "mechanical + semantic" severity P1 adr "Amendments (v1.1) §3"
  requirement STRUCT-DERIVED-001 "Derived/generated output is distinguishable from hand-authored source (excluded build dir, generated marker, or clearly-derived path)." class "mechanical + semantic" severity P1 adr "Amendments (v1.1) §2 + Invariants (render byte-identity)"
  requirement STRUCT-EXCLUDE-001 "The do-not-touch set (.cdd/, .cn-sigma/, heldout/) is excluded from content classification, never flagged as misplaced content." class mechanical severity P0 adr "Do NOT touch"
  requirement STRUCT-REFUSE-001 "When the ADR does not decide a path's home, the CM returns UNDERDETERMINED for that path and does not assign a plane." class process severity P0 adr "Deferred — foundation bundle"
  requirement STRUCT-REPAIR-001 "A repair run changes only findings in scope and preserves meaning; a move commit changes no document's meaning (evidence-boundary rule)." class process severity P0 adr "Invariants (\"No meaning change, not no edits\")"
  requirement STRUCT-REVIEW-001 "A COHERENT_WITHIN_DECLARED_SCOPE claim requires an independent full-scope review, separate from the repair actor." class process severity P0 adr "Parent RCM-BOUNDARY-001"

  # STRUCT-LIFECYCLE-001 was retired at v0.1 (ids are permanent, never reused).
  retired STRUCT-LIFECYCLE-001 "Retired at v0.1; never reused. Its dimensions returned under fresh ids STRUCT-DERIVED-001 (v1.1 §2) and STRUCT-HISTLABEL-001 (v1.1 §3); cross-plane name-predictiveness remains declined."

  disowns "policy (the ADR is the sole authority on placement, naming, function, lifecycle)", "repair (moves, renames, deletes)", "independent review closure"

  boundary note "The CM observes, classifies, and emits findings; it moves, renames, and deletes nothing. Measure → freeze the receipt → repair on a later commit → re-run → independent full-scope review closes (STRUCT-REPAIR-001, STRUCT-REVIEW-001, parent RCM-BOUNDARY-001)."
}
